# Push Workflow

Always work on `main`. There is no `staging` branch.

Ordinary editing is not permission to release. If the user says **commit only**, **just commit**, or **do not deploy**, commit or stop as asked and do not run `npm run ship` or `npm run deploy`.

## Default: "push"

When the user says **push** (or "push all branches"), run this exact workflow — not a bare `git push`:

1. **Commit** all local changes on `main` (stage everything relevant, write a clear commit message)
2. **Push and deploy** `main` using `npm run ship`. Inspect `scripts/deploy.mjs` first. It runs `git push -u origin main`, cancels pending Git builds only for that exact commit, deploys through the cached Vercel CLI path, and verifies `https://www.digitangels.com` is READY. A commit already live is not rebuilt.

Do not skip the commit step. There is no staging merge — work and deploy from `main` only.

## Variants

- Any other phrasing (e.g. "just commit", "merge only", "do not deploy") — follow exactly what they specify

When in doubt, bare **push** means commit on `main`, push that commit to GitHub, and deploy it to Vercel with `npm run ship`. Do not stop at `git push`.
